# Rate Limiting Demo
# Run: ntnt intent check server.tnt

## Overview
Per-key limits with check_limit: one contact message per email per hour.
The second message from the same email gets 429 with Retry-After.

## Glossary

| Term | Means |
|------|-------|
| someone sends a message as {body} | POST /contact body {body} |
| it is accepted | status 200 |
| it is rate limited | status 429 |
| they are told when to retry | header "retry-after" exists |
| the limit is reported | header "ratelimit-limit" equals "1" |

---

Feature: Contact rate limit
  id: feature.contact_rate_limit
  description: "One message per email per hour"

  # Scenarios run in order against one server process, so the second
  # scenario sees the budget the first one spent (one request per scenario).

  Scenario: First message from an email is accepted
    When someone sends a message as {"email": "visitor@example.test"}
    → it is accepted
    → body contains "Thanks"

  Scenario: Second message from the same email is limited
    When someone sends a message as {"email": "visitor@example.test"}
    → it is rate limited
    → they are told when to retry
    → the limit is reported

  Scenario: The same mailbox with a different domain case shares the budget
    When someone sends a message as {"email": "visitor@EXAMPLE.test"}
    → it is rate limited

  Scenario: A different email has its own budget
    When someone sends a message as {"email": "other@example.test"}
    → it is accepted
